      "content": "I hear you on the transparency part, but we aren't talking about a total fabrication. If we just note that \"spectroscopic analysis shows some variations consistent with later-period stabilization/conservation,\" we are being technically accurate without blowing the whole thing up and scaring off the big collectors. \n\nIf we wait for a full chemistry report, the Q4 auction will be over and the momentum is gone. Can't you just give me a formal assessment that acknowledges the findings as \"restoration-related\" so we can keep the lot on the books? It feels like we're overcomplicating a standard situation.",
